+{"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M1MGBADZ7AJX5SV305G7KEBC","node":"planner","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-03T20:48:44Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"Planner file tools are fs_hide-blocked on `.fabro/` (read_file and grep both return 'hidden from this stage') while shell `ls`/`rg` still reach the tree — I had to fall back to shell to verify a seed's premise against `.fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/evidence.nu`. Either grant the planner read access to the dev-loop tree its seed descriptions constantly reference, or hide it consistently including shell; the current split makes fs_hide advisory. Run 01M1MGBADZ7AJX5SV305G7KEBC."}],"observations":["Tracker holds 48 ready seeds (18 High, 30 Medium), all unblocked; sd ready orders newest-first within priority, which is not an importance signal — planner must still check premises before picking.","fabro-1e9f's per-seed claim-base machinery (seed-claim-base + per-seed diff-section) already exists in `.fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/evidence.nu` (~lines 159-290) — that seed looks stale and is a verification-only candidate for a future pass.","fabro-169b instructs a one-line edit in `workflow.fabro`, but commit 0cdc227 migrated develop+revisor run behavior to `workflow.toml` — whoever plans that seed must reconcile the target file first.","fabro-4b57 was picked as first High in sd ready with its premise verified present and its feature confirmed absent (loop-churn-section is counts-only); no review verdict was pending this pass."]}}
